  "description": "Subject: IPv6 Route Configuration \u2013 2001:db8::/64  \n\nThe IPv6 route\u202f2001:db8::/64 is set up as a **STATIC** entry (routetype\u202fSTATIC) and is currently **active** with advertising **ENABLED**. Although the \u201cStatic\u201d flag itself is **false**, the route is marked as **connected** and not **dynamic**, with a cost metric of **10**, a distance of **20**, and a weight of **1**. It resides on **VLAN\u202f100** and **VXLAN\u202f5000**, and the gateway is **fe80::1** (named **gw1**). The owner group for this route is **group1**, and the route is **not permanent**, **not a RA route**, and has a retain count of **0**. Protocol flags are all cleared: **BGP**, **OSPFv3**, **ISIS**, and **RIP** are **disabled**, and the generic **flags** field is **false**. The auxiliary data flag is **off**, while **data1** is set to **ENABLED**, and the **detail** view is enabled.  \n\nMonitoring is performed via **ping**, with a monitor status code of **0** and all three monitor parameters at **0**. So far the route has seen **0** failed probes (both per\u2011interval and total), and a total of **5** probes have been recorded. The overall state code is **1**, with a TD value of **0**, and the **type** flag is **true**.  \n\nAll other attributes (failedprobes, totalfailedprobes, retain, etc.) remain at their default zero or false settings, confirming that the route is stable and operating as intended."
